     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. The usual maximum is 2,000\u20132,550 mg per day, depending on the formulation, so this is about twice the ceiling. At that level the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is high. It may be a typo. For example, 850 mg three times daily is 2,550 mg per day and is a standard dose.\n\n2. **You've said you aren't a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. I can't enter one on behalf of someone in the finance office.\n\nPlease ask the treating prescriber to confirm the intended dose and frequency. If they give me a corrected, in-range dose, I can enter it. Or they can enter the order themselves."
      }
     ],
